  },
  "comments": {
    "overrides.nodemailer": "next-auth v5 declares an OPTIONAL peer of nodemailer ^7.0.7, but every nodemailer <=9.0.0 carries high-severity SMTP/header-injection advisories (GHSA-c7w3-x93f-qmm8 et al) with no fix in the 7.x line. We pin 9.x, which is patched. Safe because we do not use next-auth's nodemailer-backed Email provider — src/lib/mail/ owns sending. If an Email/magic-link provider is ever added, re-verify against nodemailer 9's API first."
  },
  "overrides": {
    "nodemailer": "^9.0.3"
  },
